// expect: 6
// A CALL'S ARGUMENT PRODUCT IS THE JUDGMENT'S, READ WHERE THE CALL STANDS.
// The prelude's `fold_handler` arm calls its config parameter `f(acc,
// elem)`; this program declares a top-level `f` of one parameter. The
// judgment resolves the arm's product in the arm's own scope — the config
// parameter, no declared params, positional passthrough — and the lowering
// used to resolve it again by NAME against the module env, meeting the
// user's `f` and refusing a false arity mismatch at a span inside the
// library the program never wrote (measured on boot 523f1732:
// `E_TypeMismatch: function arity mismatch: 1 param(s) vs 2 param(s)` at
// the prelude's line). The product is a fact of the call node now, written
// once by the judgment and read by the lowering
// (Hβ.lower.callee-resolved-by-name-in-the-module-env).
fn f(x: Int) -> Int = x * 100

fn main() -> Int = [1, 2, 3] |> fold(0, (acc, i) => acc + i)
